Shows exactly what would stop, asks, stops it gracefully and checks the port is free. A bare port means TCP.

Usage:
  portly stop <port> ... [flags]

Examples:
  portly stop 8000                  ask, then stop
  portly stop 3000 8000             several, one question
  portly stop 5353/udp              a UDP port
  portly stop 8000 --yes            do not ask
  portly stop 8000 --force          graceful first, then ask again and kill
  portly stop 8000 --json           show the targets and a plan_id, stop nothing

Flags:
      --expect string   stop only if the targets match this plan_id
      --force           kill if a graceful stop fails or none exists, after asking again
  -h, --help            help for stop
  -y, --yes             do not ask, every check still runs

Global Flags:
      --json      print one JSON document
      --verbose   print diagnostics on stderr
